  "name": "Example: Geometric Interpretation of the Roots of Unity",
  "problem": "Sketch a diagram showing all the $4$th roots of unity.",
  "worked_solution": "Geometrically, the $4$th roots of unity have the following properties:\n\n- all of them lie on the unit circle centered in the origin,\n\n- one of the roots is $1,$ corresponding to the point $(1,0)$ on the complex plane,\n\n- the roots form a square (regular $4$-sided polygon).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/assets/9111f21143412d791b0195722da4f6d461444f386efd9baf609c70a4fe709fd8.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
